# fig_regime_map

**Claim carried:** C7: regime map of gain / no gain / worse / invalid, including cells where every method fails.

**Shows:** one marker per cell: outcome of the headline T1 arm (select, config regime_method) against PPI++ at the same n; left, the nine real sets at every n of the reference grid and the monotone-transform stress sets; right, the failure cells (labels selected on X, Y or f; plankton shift; rare events). Cells by outcome: {'all fail': 57, 'no gain': 35, 'undecided': 10, 'gain': 8, 'invalid': 3}. No cell is classed ['worse'] and those markers are left out of the legend. The reference is the package PPI++ (`ppi-python` 0.2.3, which clips the estimated tuning to [0, 1]). Against the unclipped PPI++ the class of the headline arm changes in 7 headline cell(s) (headline.csv): alphafold n=30: no gain to small / undecided; census income n=100: no gain to small / undecided; forest n=100: small / undecided to no gain; gene expr. n=100: gain to small / undecided; gene expr. n=300: small / undecided to no gain; gene expr. n=500: small / undecided to no gain; plankton n=30: small / undecided to no gain.

**How to read:** green circle = valid and the CI upper bound of the paired ratio below 0.95; grey square = valid and the CI inside the pre-fixed no-gain margin [0.98, 1.02]; orange triangle = valid and longer, CI above 1.02; white diamond = valid, CI neither inside the margin nor below 0.95; red cross = the arm misses the pre-registered win rule (coverage); black cross = PPI++ misses it too (at small n the PPI++ Wald interval itself under-covers, so a red or black cross there is partly the reference's failure).

